Z||000000||My7Fieros||07-20-2001||03:01 AM||||Ok some of you AOL users may already know this, but its new to me...wish I had my camera to take a pic, but youll see when you do it.<BR>Go up to your tool bar up top and pick one of the icon things you can live without (I used the $ emblem, but you can use calender or whatever you want). Right click on it then click on where it says "remove from toolbar"..then bring up the Fiero Forum main page (or whatever website you frequent the most) and drag the heart in the upper right hand corner to the (now blank) location where the icon you deleted once was.<BR>A box w/ several different icons will appear..choose the one you want, then type in a name in the name box. Voila! You now have a direct link to the forum (or whatever site you chose) on your toolbar!<BR>I used the car emblem and typed "Fiero". Pretty neat feature....no more hunting through the favorites section. It only takes a few seconds! P.S. I know this works on version 6.0...but Im not sure if it'll work on 4.0 or 5.0...any 4 or 5.0 users try it out and lemme know. Thanx.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||10
